1
00:00:00,330 --> 00:00:02,420
Every AI you know talks.

2
00:00:02,860 --> 00:00:04,710
Ask it anything, and it writes you a

3
00:00:04,730 --> 00:00:05,360
paragraph.

4
00:00:05,900 --> 00:00:07,320
This one can't chat.

5
00:00:07,690 --> 00:00:09,120
It won't even write code.

6
00:00:09,540 --> 00:00:12,250
It's called Jev, from a San Francisco lab

7
00:00:12,270 --> 00:00:14,860
called TypeSafe, and it's gone viral.

8
00:00:15,250 --> 00:00:17,170
Jev only makes decisions.

9
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:19,340
Give it the facts and a question,

10
00:00:19,410 --> 00:00:21,130
and it answers with a probability.

11
00:00:21,540 --> 00:00:23,490
Pick an option, give a score,

12
00:00:23,510 --> 00:00:24,730
or say yes or no,

13
00:00:24,750 --> 00:00:25,910
and how sure it is.

14
00:00:26,430 --> 00:00:27,530
An email comes in:

15
00:00:27,870 --> 00:00:29,840
billing, technical or account?

16
00:00:30,150 --> 00:00:32,500
Jev picks one, with its confidence.

17
00:00:32,840 --> 00:00:35,230
If it's sure, your software acts.

18
00:00:35,430 --> 00:00:37,210
If not, a person takes over.

19
00:00:37,730 --> 00:00:40,020
TypeSafe calls it a System One model,

20
00:00:40,290 --> 00:00:42,880
named after fast, gut-feeling thinking.

21
00:00:43,220 --> 00:00:44,850
By TypeSafe's own test,

22
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:48,760
it's 193 times faster than a typical LLM,

23
00:00:48,780 --> 00:00:51,850
and 444 times cheaper.

24
00:00:52,320 --> 00:00:55,450
Input costs 42 dollars per billion tokens.

25
00:00:55,850 --> 00:00:57,340
The answers are free.

26
00:00:57,690 --> 00:00:59,720
Developers use it to route tickets and

27
00:00:59,740 --> 00:01:01,050
police AI agents.

28
00:01:01,550 --> 00:01:03,380
Someone even made it play Doom.

29
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:06,470
The catch: it only answers what you ask,

30
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:08,120
from the options you give,

31
00:01:08,420 --> 00:01:09,860
and it can still be wrong.

32
00:01:10,310 --> 00:01:11,310
And it's closed:

33
00:01:11,800 --> 00:01:14,340
API only, and those numbers are the

34
00:01:14,360 --> 00:01:15,260
company's own.

35
00:01:15,690 --> 00:01:17,820
Still, the idea is big.

36
00:01:18,260 --> 00:01:20,190
An AI that doesn't talk.

37
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:21,550
It just decides.

38
00:01:22,090 --> 00:01:23,350
That's today's tool.

39
00:01:23,590 --> 00:01:26,140
Subscribe, there's a new one every day.
